welcome to your new favorite Call of  Duty playlist war brought to you by Call  of Duty World War 2 war is an all-new  multiplayer game mode where players must  work as a team to defeat the enemy it's  an immersive narrative driven experience  that pits Allied and Axis forces against  each other in team driven assault and  defend missions set within iconic World  War 2 locations each match is divided  into two rounds with you alternating  roles between the Allies and axis your  mission changes depending on which side  you find yourself on typically with one  side acting as the aggressor and the  other side running defense as the  attackers you'll need to complete a  string of objectives against the clock  each requiring close cooperation and  adaptive tactics naturally it's the  defenders job to do everything in their  power to keep those objectives  unfulfilled and the clock ticking all  the way down to zero  war absorbs elements from a variety of  popular modes and amalgamates them into  something that feels completely new  within just one game you'll capture and  hold zones in similar fashion to  domination and hardpoint construct Sambi  style defensive walls and gun nests  indulge in some search and destroy bomb  defusal and even a score to payload in  scenes reminiscent of safeguard there  are also elements completely unique as a  war including some seriously hazardous  bridge building now let's get one thing  out of the way regardless of your skill  level you will die and there's every  chance that you'll die a lot this is a  mode that forces you to move beyond KD  ratios and score streaks because there's  far more important things at stake so  leave your lone wolf instincts at the  door and prepare to make some heroic  sacrifices for the good of the squad  which brings us to our first tip for  success communication obviously this is  a mode best suited for party play and  the ability to react and respond to  enemy tactics as a unit rests on your  ability to coordinate with the rest of  your team as each objective is focused  on a small chunk of a large map calling  out enemy positions and objective  locations in the heat of combat is much  more easily done than other modes if  chat is impossible pay close attention  to the in-game dialogue which reacts  intelligently to situations and observes  the roles of your teammates of playing  so that you can provide useful support  if somebody's taking the risk to perform  some construction be the one to lay down  covering fire so their efforts aren't in  vain or if a zone is being captured aim  to defend any potential flanking  positions war is also a great reason to  have a loadout slot dedicated to each  division a shotgun or SMG might be  perfectly suited for close quarters  engagements when capturing a building  but are near useless when you're  separated by a trench as with all other  modes matching the weapons your choice  of division means your gun will receive  a vital additional perk which can make  all the difference the same thinking  applies to your grenades never before  has a smoke grenade been such an  essential part of your loadout as it's  the perfect means of obfuscating and  objective and making it that much  harder for the opposition to get their  sights trained on you as you become  better acquainted with the various maps  you can start to have a loadout suited  to each objective and switch between  them when the occasion calls for it  although you will have to suffer a noble  death for the change to take effect  although you won't be earning any  scorestreaks you will receive additional  aid from air drops these acts just like  care packages in normal multiplayer  modes but the reward is fixed and  tailored to the map the major difference  here is that the perk remains in your  armory until the gas or ammo runs out so  if you're quick enough to nab that  flamethrower you'll keep it after you  respawn just don't fool yourself into  thinking that they'll make you  unstoppable finally if you ever find  yourself escorting a tank that armored  payload isn't just for show while the  tank movements is automated the gun  turret is up for grabs and grants you  awesome firepower for as long as you can  avoid being shot the obvious trade-off  is that you're completely out in the  open and a good six feet higher than  usual so your enemies will see you  coming a mile off watch your head  war is a mode that rewards players and  teams who work smart think on their  boots and exploit the environment to  their advantage most importantly though  it's fresh frantic and fun and will  force even the most battle-hardened Call  of Duty veteran to completely rethink  the way they play  [Music]  you
 

